      "etymology": {
        "text": "derives from the Latin name <em>Francia, </em>meaning \"Land of the Franks\"; the Franks were a group of Germanic tribes located along the middle and lower Rhine River in the 3rd century A.D.; the origin of the tribal name is unclear but may come from the Old German word <em>franka</em>, meaning \"brave,\" or from a personal name such as Francio or Francus"
